# ADR 0003 - Visibility Based On Observation

## Context

The first implementation considered blocks exposed when
touching air or fluids.

Production analysis showed that physical contact does not
always represent player visibility.

Examples:

- ores behind lava;
- ores separated by walls;
- ores visible through glass.

## Decision

AntiXray visibility must be based on player observation,
not only block adjacency.

A block is visible when the player has a valid observation path
under normal gameplay conditions.

## Consequences

Positive:

- fewer false reveals;
- closer to real player experience.

Negative:

- requires additional visibility analysis.
